<text x="-5.8" y="-88" dominant-baseline="central" text-anchor="start" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#b91c1c" stroke="#f8fafc" stroke-width="4" paint-order="stroke" stroke-linejoin="round">OH</text>
</svg>', 'The –OH group is a strong activator and ortho/para director (lone pair donation). In polar bromine water no Lewis acid is needed, and substitution continues at all three activated positions (2, 4 and 6), giving the white precipitate of 2,4,6-tribromophenol.', 'A');
