<text x="146.6" y="-88" dominant-baseline="central" text-anchor="start" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#b91c1c" stroke="#f8fafc" stroke-width="4" paint-order="stroke" stroke-linejoin="round">O</text>
</svg>', 'All 9 carbons are sp²: 6 in the benzene ring, 2 in the C=C, and 1 in the C=O (carbonyl carbon). π bonds: 3 in the ring (Kekulé) + 1 C=C + 1 C=O = 5. There is no sp³ or sp carbon, so the whole molecule is planar and conjugated.', 'A');
